h confidence, but explicitly notes that imaging analysis is **not a definitive diagnostic tool**.\n- **Summary:** the pipeline suggests a **high likelihood of kidney cancer** and says the visual evidence is consistent with a **kidney tumor**.\n- **Visual evidence:** the analysis reports detection of a kidney tumor–like region.\n- **Recommended next steps:**\n  1. Further medical evaluation, including imaging and lab tests, to confirm the finding.\n  2. Consultation with a medical professional to discuss the result.\n  3. Consider additional diagnostic testing such as biopsy or genetic testing if clinically appropriate.\n\n**References**\n- *Kidney Cancer: Diagnosis and Treatment* — American Cancer Society (2022)  \n  https://www.cancer.org/cancer/kidney-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging.html\n- *Imaging in Kidney Cancer* — European Association of Urology (2020)  \n  https://uroweb.org/guideline/kidney-cancer/\n\n**Important:** this is a **preliminary pipeline signal, not a diagnosis**. A radiologist/urologist should interpret the full CT study and clinical context.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg\n\nIf you want, I can also give you:\n- a **short patient-friendly explanation**, or\n- the **raw JSON output** from the pipeline.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_01841bdf8066d3e80169bd935152208191b24e92b011476c7c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10549,"output":548,"cacheRead":23680,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34777,"cost":{"input":0.026372500000000004,"output":0.00822,"cacheRead":0.00592,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.04051250000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774031692634}}
